.TH garuda-toolbox-users-add 1  "garuda-toolbox 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
garuda\-toolbox\-users\-add \- Create an account and set its password, at once
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgaruda\-toolbox users add\fR [\fB\-\-full\-name\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-shell\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-admin\fR] [\fB\-\-group\fR \fIGROUP\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR \fIWHEN\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-width\fR \fICOLUMNS\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIUSER\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create an account and set its password, at once
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-full\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
The person\*(Aqs full name
.TP
\fB\-\-shell\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
The login shell, one of /etc/shells. Without it useradd\*(Aqs default
.TP
\fB\-\-admin\fR
May install software and change the system (the group wheel)
.TP
\fB\-\-group\fR \fI<GROUP>\fR
A further group, as often as needed
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR
Read the password from the first line of standard input instead of asking on the terminal
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print the programs\*(Aq own words under an error
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Print long text directly instead of through `$PAGER`
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Do not ask, carry the change out. Needed without a terminal
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Colour the output: auto, always or never
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the plan and stop, without asking and without changing anything
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON Lines instead of text, for scripts. Needs `\-\-yes` or `\-\-dry\-run`
.TP
\fB\-\-width\fR \fI<COLUMNS>\fR
Cut long cells to this many columns
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Leave out the spinner and the hints
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIUSER\fR>
The new account\*(Aqs name: small letters, digits, hyphens and underscores, at most 32 characters
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  garuda\-toolbox users add ada \-\-full\-name "Ada Lovelace" \-\-admin
  printf \*(Aq%s\\n\*(Aq "$PW" | garuda\-toolbox users add ci \-\-password\-stdin \-\-yes
.SH "SEE ALSO"
garuda\-toolbox\-users(1), garuda\-toolbox(1)
